<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  schneider_cell.urdf.xacro  -  V44 (release 2 cm, lateral grasp, no
                                      magic orientation, smaller rivet cabin,
                                      bins right, vision left)
  ===========================================================================
  V44 SUMMARY (deltas vs V43):
   * Release height SHRUNK from +100 mm to +20 mm above the cradle
     base (POSE_RELEASE_LOAD_FIXTURE, POSE_RELEASE_VISION).  CAFI now
     falls only 20 mm under gravity to settle into the seat.
   * Lateral grasp: IK targets shifted by 0.030 m along the gripper's
     LOCAL +Y closing direction at PICK/PLACE so the moving appendage
     jaw clamps the CAFI from one lateral side (not from the centre
     between the jaws).  Implementation: two-pass IK in resolve_poses.py.
   * Object manager settling: XY snap clamp tightened from 100 mm to
     5 mm.  Seat orientation override REMOVED so the CAFI keeps the
     orientation it had at release (no magic rotation).
   * Rivet cabin SHRUNK: cabin_size 0.700x0.400 -> 0.450x0.300,
     cabin_height 0.500 -> 0.350.  South edge of canopy now 0.200 m
     north of the LOAD seat (vs 0.000 m before), so the cobot wrist
     no longer collides with the canopy at any LOAD-related pose.
   * Bins moved EAST: aceptado (1.580, 0.679) -> (1.650, 0.720);
     rechazado (1.320, 0.684) -> (1.330, 0.720).  Separation widened
     from 260 mm to 320 mm (93 mm clear between walls).  Both still
     inside the L03S reach with 29 mm / 252 mm of margin.
   * Vision fixture + camera + sensor shifted 74 mm WEST: from x=0.824
     to x=0.750.  Reach margin 155 mm; no impact on existing vision
     pose quality.
   * Per-joint mesa clearance check added to pose_collision_checker
     V44: every joint origin world Z must be > 1.000 + 5 mm at every
     pose.
   * 19 poses re-resolved with lateral grasp + tighter release +
     new layout (resolve_poses.py).
  ===========================================================================
  V43 SUMMARY (deltas vs V42):
   * The cobot is now the user-supplied URDF
     /home/student/planta Schneider/lexium_cobot_with_final_gripper_z_reference.zip
     mounted unchanged in kinematics, joint origins, axes, rpy and joint
     limits.  joint_2 rpy="0 0 0.05" comes back (V36-A's zero-out is
     reverted because the user URDF ships that 2.86 deg CAD skew).
   * Gripper is now PART OF the cobot URDF (5 STLs + prismatic
     appendage_prismatic_joint + tcp_link at the working centre).  The
     old new_gripper.xacro is NO LONGER included or instantiated.
   * Logical TCP frame the planta uses: lexium_cobot_tcp_grasp_center
     (alias for tcp_link inside the cobot xacro), addressed by FK, IK,
     object manager, gripper sim, collision filter, pick/place
     trajectories.
   * RELEASE_LOAD_FIXTURE and RELEASE_VISION pose entries added so the
     gripper releases the CAFI 100 mm ABOVE the cradle base (user spec).
   * NEMA + belt already on the RIGHT of the disc (link X=+0.244,
     world (0.936, 1.259)) — V41/V42 layout preserved.
   * All 19 IK-resolved poses re-validated against the new TCP offset
     (resolve_poses.py + validate_robot_poses.txt: 19/19 PASS;
     pose_collision_checker.py: 19/19 PASS).
  ===========================================================================
  V38 SUMMARY (only the deltas vs V37):
   * Cobot mounted DIRECTLY on the mesa, NO external pedestal: the
     canonical link0_base.STL is the real cobot base; it sits at
     world (1.252, 1.049, 1.000), centre of the mesa.
     mount_mode="floor" (Rx +pi/2) keeps the arm standing.  No more
     cabin overhead mount, no more pedestal cylinder.
   * Conveyor PICK switched to the LEFT (west) end of the belt.
     Notch on the south rail moved from local X=+0.150 to X=-0.135 so
     the cobot grabs at world (1.235, 1.365).  Suministro CAFI feeder
     moved to the EAST end of the belt; CAFIs travel east-to-west.
     sensor_conveyor_end re-aimed at the west pick.
   * Camera HANGING from cabin top profile (z=2.07) by a vertical
     column down to the body at z=1.32 (= mesa + 0.32 per spec).
     arm_length=0 -> column coaxial with body, looking straight down
     at the fixture cámara on the mesa.
   * Riveting cabin WIDER (0.700 x 0.400 vs V37's 0.400 x 0.300) so
     the 530 x 500 mm disco gearbase fits with margin and the LOAD
     side is open to the cobot.
   * V37 residue removed: cobot_reach_circle (yaml), publish_cell_
     markers.py (script + 14 old station labels), V19-V18 history
     block in scene_dimensions.yaml, V34/V33 view rviz files, old
     cycle_simulate_v36/v37.py, old evidence logs.
   * Everything else (mesa real 1.62 x 0.92 x 1.00, disco giratorio
     STL pack, gripper alignment, control station XY) is preserved
     from V37 byte-for-byte where it was correct.
  ===========================================================================
  V38 SUMMARY (only the deltas vs V37):
   * Cobot mounted DIRECTLY on the mesa, NO external pedestal: the
     canonical link0_base.STL is the real cobot base; it sits at
     world (1.252, 1.049, 1.000), centre of the mesa.
     mount_mode="floor" (Rx +pi/2) keeps the arm standing.  No more
     cabin overhead mount, no more pedestal cylinder.
   * Conveyor PICK switched to the LEFT (west) end of the belt.
     Notch on the south rail moved from local X=+0.150 to X=-0.135 so
     the cobot grabs at world (1.235, 1.365).  Suministro CAFI feeder
     moved to the EAST end of the belt; CAFIs travel east-to-west.
     sensor_conveyor_end re-aimed at the west pick.
   * Camera HANGING from cabin top profile (z=2.07) by a vertical
     column down to the body at z=1.32 (= mesa + 0.32 per spec).
     arm_length=0 -> column coaxial with body, looking straight down
     at the fixture cámara on the mesa.
   * Riveting cabin WIDER (0.700 x 0.400 vs V37's 0.400 x 0.300) so
     the 530 x 500 mm disco gearbase fits with margin and the LOAD
     side is open to the cobot.
   * V37 residue removed: cobot_reach_circle (yaml), publish_cell_
     markers.py (script + 14 old station labels), V19-V18 history
     block in scene_dimensions.yaml, V34/V33 view rviz files, old
     cycle_simulate_v36/v37.py, old evidence logs.
   * Everything else (mesa real 1.62 x 0.92 x 1.00, disco giratorio
     STL pack, gripper alignment, control station XY) is preserved
     from V37 byte-for-byte where it was correct.
  ===========================================================================
  V37 SUMMARY (kept for diff context):
   * Layout XY re-imported from PlantaSchneiderReal.dxf (1 mm = 0.001 m).
     DXF mesa outline (1620 x 920 mm) is anchored in world so its
     centre still sits at (1.252, 1.049) - V36 frame preserved.
   * Cobot NO LONGER hangs.  Floor-mounted on a 0.55 m pedestal column
     (radius 0.060 m) at world (0.950, 0.972).  mount_mode="floor"
     applies Rx(+pi/2) so the canonical CAD +Y arm-axis maps to
     world +Z (cobot stands up).  yaw=0 leaves the arm reaching
     toward world +X.
   * Process platform REMOVED.  Cobot reaches mesa-top items directly
     from the pedestal (mesa top z=1.000; cobot tool0 q=0 at z=1.018).
   * Disco giratorio REBUILT with 15 STLs from disco giratorio.zip.
     STL inspection confirmed Z is already the vertical axis in the
     exported meshes - the URDF applies IDENTITY rotation per visual.
     Disc centre placed at DXF (250.1, 670) mm -> world (0.692, 1.259).
     Disco_1 face top at z=1.081 (mesa top + 0.081).
   * Conveyor at DXF (927.5, 775.7) mm -> world (1.370, 1.365), size
     0.375 x 0.150, belt top z=1.070.
   * Aceptado/Rechazado bins at world (1.411, 0.679) and (1.110, 0.684)
     per DXF #38 and #37, bin floor on mesa top (z=1.000).
   * Fixture cámara at world (0.824, 0.804) per DXF #46.  Cognex camera
     body directly above at z=1.320 (= mesa top + 0.320 per spec).
   * Estación de control at world (0.684, 0.462), OUTSIDE the mesa
     to the south (DXF #39).
   * Gripper alignment UNCHANGED: tool0 -> gripper_mount transform
     preserved (mount_xyz "0 -0.014 0", mount_rpy "-pi/2 0 0",
     mount_yaw=pi).  SolidWorks 99.5 mm reference still maps to
     link -Y; jaw tip lands at world height tool0_z - 0.083 m.
   * Aluminum cabin kept as a decorative enclosure (cobot does NOT
     hang from it any more).  Cabin posts span world floor to z=2.07.
  ===========================================================================
  V36 (PREVIOUS) doc retained below for historical context:
  ======================================================================
  schneider_cell.urdf.xacro  -  V36 (real-planta dimensions, hanging
                                      cobot at top profile, process
                                      platform elevated on mesa)
  ===========================================================================
  V36 CHANGES vs V35:
    * MESA = real Schneider planta dimensions: 1.62 m x 0.92 m,
        top surface z = 1.00 m.  Centred at world (1.600, 0.700)
        directly under the cobot anchor.
    * ALUMINUM CABIN rebuilt with REAL 50 x 50 mm aluminum profiles
        (V35 used 45 mm).  Structure top at world z = 2.07 m; top
        profile bottom face = 2.02 m (where cobot mounting flange
        bolts on).
    * PROCESS PLATFORM 2.00 x 1.50 m steel plate at top_z = 1.20 m,
        sits 0.20 m above mesa.  Mesa supports the central 1.62 x
        0.92 m overlap; 4 corner posts carry the overhanging area.
        All V35 process station XY/Z preserved (BELT_TOP=1.277,
        LOAD_SEAT=1.312, VISION_TOP=1.250, BIN_FLOOR=1.205).
        Platform height chosen by FK/IK: with cobot anchor at
        z=2.02 m the IK reaches every target with |q|<2 rad and
        0.1 mm Cartesian error.
    * COBOT anchor: world z 2.350 -> 2.020 (real top profile underside).
        Anchor XY (1.600, 0.700) preserved.  Rx(-pi/2): CAD +Y -> -Z.
    * HOME redefined: J1=0, J2=0, J3=0, J4=-pi/2, J5=-pi/2, J6=0
        (real planta HOME).  V35 used q=0 — now obsolete.
    * GRIPPER mount realigned per SolidWorks 99.5 mm Z reference:
        mount_xyz="0 -0.014 0", mount_yaw=pi.  Stump bottom-face
        centre now coincident with tool0 origin (flange face).
    * CANONICAL URDF correction V36-A: joint_2 rpy "0 0 0.05" -> "0 0 0"
        (was a 2.86 deg CAD measurement skew producing the small
        visible wobble in V32..V35).
  ===========================================================================
  V23 (historic) doc: CAD-faithful fixture, IK-validated cobot poses,
                      grasp_center at the tip.
  ===========================================================================
  V23 CHANGES (vs V22 untouched layout):
    * fixture_rivet.xacro rebuilt from the user's SolidWorks assembly
      meshes.  Each fixture now has EXACTLY 2 lateral solenoids (real
      EnsamblajePISTONGOOD mesh + mirrored instance), the top SOLENOID
      mesh is no longer instantiated in the fixture (it belongs to the
      riveting station above), and the rivet hammer joint is kept with
      no visual link so the rotary_fixture_sim controller does not see
      an unknown joint.
    * new_gripper.xacro: grasp_center moved from link Z=-0.075 to
      link Z=+0.085 so the frame lands at the gripper tip (link +Z is
      world -Z under the default tool0 orientation).  This is the single
      change that lets the V23 geometric grasp work again; V20-V22
      had the frame on the wrong side, which is why the V22 task-aware
      grasp shortcut was invented as a workaround.
    * No mesh moved, no link moved, no joint name changed in any other
      component (lexium_cobot_real, plant_table, conveyor, vision,
      cognex_2800, control_station, sensors, drives, pneumatics).
  ===========================================================================
  Original V20 doc below.

  schneider_cell.urdf.xacro  -  V20  (REAL fixture on disc, prismatic jaw,
                                      bigger disc, NO disc_anvil substitute,
                                      NO stand-alone press)
  ===========================================================================
  V20 architectural changes (vs V19) at the URDF level:

    [A] DISC REDESIGN
        - disc_radius   0.180 -> 0.310   (620 mm diameter)
        - mount_radius  0.150 -> 0.230   (460 mm centre-to-centre, fits
                                          the REAL 297 mm fixture)
        - LOAD mount (outer, cobot side): world (1.671, 1.145, 1.220)
        - RIVET mount (inner, press side): world (1.671, 1.605, 1.220)
        - Cobot-to-LOAD distance = 0.225 m (well inside 0.626 m reach)

    [B] REAL FIXTURE ON THE DISC
        - V19 disc_anvil.xacro is GONE (file removed).
        - Two copies of the REAL `fixture_rivet` (user's rivet_final
          assembly) instanced on the disc.  The two LATERAL solenoids
          + the TOP piston are now per-fixture moving joints.
        - V19 stand-alone rivet_press_stand + rivet_press_assembly are
          REMOVED.  The rivet press IS the on-disc fixture.
        - Cabin geometry preserved (include_press=false stays).

    [C] PRISMATIC JAW IN GRIPPER
        - new_gripper.xacro now has a 5th visual link (`gripper_base_jaw`)
          connected with `gripper_base_jaw_joint` (prismatic, axis +X,
          range [-0.016, 0.000]).
        - The fictitious Marker.CUBE jaws of V19 are GONE (process
          markers no longer render proxy jaws).

    [D] PISTON RPY CORRECTED
        - gripper_pneumatics sub-anchor rpy V19 (0, +pi/2, 0) -> V20
          (0, -pi/2, 0).  Same axis (Ry), opposite sign.  Cluster stays
          inside the housing without protrusion.

  Cobot kinematics: byte-for-byte V15..V19 (lexium_cobot_real unchanged).
  V20 publishes joints J1..J6 PLUS the disc joint, jaw joint, fixture
  piston/solenoids joints via the schneider_robot_controller +
  schneider_gripper_sim + schneider_rotary_fixture_sim nodes.
-->
<robot name="schneider_cell" xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">

  <xacro:arg name="scene_yaml" default=""/>

  <!-- ===== component libraries (V20: no disc_anvil) ================== -->
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/materials.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/plant_table.xacro"/>
  <!-- V38: process_platform.xacro removed (process platform deleted in V37). -->
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/workstation.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/conveyor.xacro"/>
  <!-- V52: fixture_rivet.xacro REMOVED.  The rivet fixtures are now part
       of the new turntable_rivet_cell URDF (rivet_fixture_1_link +
       rivet_fixture_2_link with their fixed pistons). -->
  <!-- <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/fixture_rivet.xacro"/> -->
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/fixture_vision.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/cafi.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/cognex_2800.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/lexium_cobot_real.xacro"/>
  <!-- V30: aluminum cabin frame that supports the hanging cobot. -->
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/aluminum_cabin.xacro"/>
  <!-- V43: gripper is now PART OF the cobot URDF
       (lexium_cobot_with_final_gripper.xacro).  The old new_gripper.xacro
       is no longer included or instantiated. -->
  <!-- <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/new_gripper.xacro"/> -->
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/riveting_station.xacro"/>
  <!-- V52: rotary_index_table_v37.xacro REMOVED.  The new turntable
       package supplies the disc, base, NEMA, belt, sensor and BOTH
       fixtures in a single URDF (turntable_rivet_cell.urdf).  We wrap
       it in a xacro macro (turntable_rivet_cell.xacro) so the planta
       mounts it with a SINGLE fixed transform without touching the
       internal layout. -->
  <!-- <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/rotary_index_table_v37.xacro"/> -->
  <xacro:include filename="$(find turntable_rivet_cell_description)/urdf/turntable_rivet_cell.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/control_station.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/photoelectric_sensor_sick_grte18s_p2312.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/conveyor_motor.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/rotary_drive_nema17_planetary.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/pneumatic_supply.xacro"/>
  <!-- V22: gripper_pneumatics removed from the assembly. The file stays
       on disk for history but is NOT included. See "[Fix 3]" in
       schneider_cell_description_V22_resumen.md. -->
  <!-- <xacro:include filename="$(find schneider_cell_description)/urdf/components/gripper_pneumatics.xacro"/> -->


  <!-- ===== world root ================================================ -->
  <link name="world"/>

  <link name="cell_floor">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry><box size="2.504408 2.098121 0.005"/></geometry>
      <material name="floor_mat"/>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="world_to_cell_floor" type="fixed">
    <parent link="world"/>
    <child  link="cell_floor"/>
    <origin xyz="1.252205 1.049061 -0.0025" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ===== V36 Plant mesa (REAL Schneider planta dimensions) =========
       Long side 1.62 m (X), short side 0.92 m (Y), top surface z=1.00 m.
       Centred at the cobot anchor (1.252, 1.049) so the work envelope
       is concentric with the mesa.
       40 mm slab + 60 mm box-section legs from floor (z=0) up to the
       slab underside.                                              -->
  <xacro:plant_table name="plant_table" parent="world"
                     xy_x="1.252205" xy_y="1.049061"
                     size_x="1.620"  size_y="0.920"
                     top_z="1.000"   thickness="0.040"
                     leg_section="0.060"  leg_inset="0.060"
                     stretcher_section="0.040"/>

  <!-- V37: process platform REMOVED.  Floor-mounted cobot reaches
       directly to mesa-top items (mesa_top z=1.000, cobot tool0 q=0
       z=1.018) so the V36 0.30 m elevated platform is no longer
       needed.  Bins and stations now rest directly on mesa top.   -->

  <!-- ===== V38 Conveyor (DXF #47: 375 x 150 mm @ DXF 927.5, 775.7) ====
       World (1.370, 1.365), top-of-belt at z = mesa_top + 0.070 = 1.070.
       V38 picks on the LEFT side of the belt - notch at local X = -0.135
       on the south rail, so the rail opening is at world X = 1.235
       and the cobot grabs from the west (left) end.  Reach to that
       point from the cobot at (1.252, 1.049) is just 0.353 m.        -->
  <xacro:conveyor_section name="conveyor_1" parent="world"
                          xy_x="1.370" xy_y="1.365"
                          size_x="0.375"  size_y="0.150"
                          top_z="1.070"  body_height="0.065"
                          long_axis="x"
                          support_z="1.000"
                          notch_n_x_local="-0.135"
                          notch_n_w="0.060"/>

  <!-- ===== V38 Suministro CAFI (feeder at EAST end of belt; CAFIs are
       fed in from the east and travel west to the left-side pick).  -->
  <link name="suministro_cafi">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry><box size="0.150 0.220 0.015"/></geometry>
      <material name="feeder_top"/>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="world_to_suministro_cafi" type="fixed">
    <parent link="world"/>
    <child  link="suministro_cafi"/>
    <origin xyz="1.620 1.365 1.0075" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ===== Quality bins (preserved) ================================== -->
  <xacro:macro name="hollow_bin"
               params="name parent xy_x xy_y size_x size_y height
                       wall_t bottom_z material">
    <link name="${name}_bottom">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="${size_x} ${size_y} ${wall_t}"/></geometry>
        <material name="${material}"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="${parent}_to_${name}_bottom" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${parent}"/>
      <child  link="${name}_bottom"/>
      <origin xyz="${xy_x} ${xy_y} ${bottom_z + wall_t/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <link name="${name}_wall_n">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="${size_x} ${wall_t} ${height - wall_t}"/></geometry>
        <material name="${material}"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="${name}_bottom_to_wall_n" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${name}_bottom"/>
      <child  link="${name}_wall_n"/>
      <origin xyz="0 ${ size_y/2 - wall_t/2} ${wall_t/2 + (height - wall_t)/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <link name="${name}_wall_s">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="${size_x} ${wall_t} ${height - wall_t}"/></geometry>
        <material name="${material}"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="${name}_bottom_to_wall_s" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${name}_bottom"/>
      <child  link="${name}_wall_s"/>
      <origin xyz="0 ${-size_y/2 + wall_t/2} ${wall_t/2 + (height - wall_t)/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <link name="${name}_wall_e">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="${wall_t} ${size_y - 2*wall_t} ${height - wall_t}"/></geometry>
        <material name="${material}"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="${name}_bottom_to_wall_e" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${name}_bottom"/>
      <child  link="${name}_wall_e"/>
      <origin xyz="${ size_x/2 - wall_t/2} 0 ${wall_t/2 + (height - wall_t)/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <link name="${name}_wall_w">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="${wall_t} ${size_y - 2*wall_t} ${height - wall_t}"/></geometry>
        <material name="${material}"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="${name}_bottom_to_wall_w" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${name}_bottom"/>
      <child  link="${name}_wall_w"/>
      <origin xyz="${-size_x/2 + wall_t/2} 0 ${wall_t/2 + (height - wall_t)/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
  </xacro:macro>

  <!-- V49 bins: rechazado pulled BACK INSIDE the mesa.  V48 placed it
       at (1.330, 0.580) but mesa Y range is [0.589, 1.509]; bin half-Y
       = 0.091 m so V48 spilled to Y_min=0.489 OFF the mesa.  V49
       puts rechazado at (1.330, 0.700) — 120 mm north of V48 — so the
       bin footprint Y[0.609, 0.791] sits ENTIRELY on the mesa with
       20 mm of margin to the south edge.  aceptado kept at (1.650,
       0.720) (V46 position; moving it south would push it past the
       L03S 0.626 m reach sphere).
       Reach 3D from cobot (1.152, 1.049, 1.000) to bin floor
       (z=1.005) + CAFI half-height (z=1.018):
         aceptado d = sqrt(0.498^2 + 0.329^2 + 0.018^2) = 0.597 m
         rechazado d = sqrt(0.178^2 + 0.349^2 + 0.018^2) = 0.392 m
       Both well inside the L03S 0.626 m reach.  Reject has 234 mm of
       headroom; accept has 29 mm.  Top-down access stays clean: the
       reject bin opening is centred at world (1.330, 0.700), 349 mm
       south of the cobot base, no overlap with conveyor or cabin.  -->
  <xacro:hollow_bin name="aceptado" parent="world"
                    xy_x="1.650" xy_y="0.720"
                    size_x="0.226837" size_y="0.172000"
                    height="0.150" wall_t="0.005"
                    bottom_z="1.000" material="bin_accept"/>
  <xacro:hollow_bin name="rechazado" parent="world"
                    xy_x="1.330" xy_y="0.700"
                    size_x="0.226837" size_y="0.182000"
                    height="0.150" wall_t="0.005"
                    bottom_z="1.000" material="bin_reject"/>

  <!-- ===== V56 Riveting zone anchor (disc CENTRE on mesa top) =========
       V56 shifts the disc eastward by +0.300 m so the cobot can reach
       the LOAD seat with joint5 = -pi/2 (= -90 deg) — the IK probe
       under scripts/probe_j5_reach.py shows convergent J5=-90
       solutions in the [0.25, 0.40] m range; +0.30 m is the smallest
       shift that keeps every joint comfortably inside its limit while
       leaving > 50 mm clearance between the disc rim and the cobot
       pedestal.
         old anchor: world (0.692, 1.259, 1.000)
         new anchor: world (0.992, 1.259, 1.000)         -->
  <link name="riveting_zone"/>
  <joint name="world_to_riveting_zone" type="fixed">
    <parent link="world"/>
    <child  link="riveting_zone"/>
    <origin xyz="0.992 1.259 1.000" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- V56 RIVETING INDICATOR (cabin removed).
       The user asked to drop the full riveting cabin (posts + canopy
       + lip + tray + back wall) and keep ONLY the visual indicator
       that signals whether riveting is in progress.  We replace the
       whole `riveting_station_features` macro with a small stack
       light mounted directly on the mesa next to the disc.  The
       three lamp spheres mirror the V54 cabin lamps (red / amber /
       green) and remain a static visual cue — the functional state
       is the /rivet/active topic, already surfaced on the HMI as
       DO3 Remachado.  -->
  <link name="rivet_indicator_post">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.012" length="0.300"/></geometry>
      <material name="station_pillar"/>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="riveting_zone_to_indicator_post" type="fixed">
    <parent link="riveting_zone"/>
    <child  link="rivet_indicator_post"/>
    <origin xyz="-0.220 0.000 0.150" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="rivet_indicator_lamp_red">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry><sphere radius="0.025"/></geometry>
      <material name="lamp_red"/>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="indicator_post_to_lamp_red" type="fixed">
    <parent link="rivet_indicator_post"/>
    <child  link="rivet_indicator_lamp_red"/>
    <origin xyz="0 0 0.180" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="rivet_indicator_lamp_amber">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry><sphere radius="0.025"/></geometry>
      <material name="lamp_amber"/>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="indicator_post_to_lamp_amber" type="fixed">
    <parent link="rivet_indicator_post"/>
    <child  link="rivet_indicator_lamp_amber"/>
    <origin xyz="0 0 0.130" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="rivet_indicator_lamp_green">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry><sphere radius="0.025"/></geometry>
      <material name="lamp_green"/>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="indicator_post_to_lamp_green" type="fixed">
    <parent link="rivet_indicator_post"/>
    <child  link="rivet_indicator_lamp_green"/>
    <origin xyz="0 0 0.080" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ===== V52 Turntable rivet cell (drop-in from user's package) =======
       The whole rivet station (rotating disc, NEMA + base, belt, two
       fixtures with their fixed pistons, photoelectric sensor pedestal,
       sensor body + lens + light ray, CAFI lateral target frames and
       pick frames) is supplied by turntable_rivet_cell_description's
       URDF.  We wrap it as a xacro macro and instantiate it with a
       SINGLE transform from riveting_zone.

       Internal layout is byte-for-byte the original URDF:
         - base_link is fixed to riveting_zone (does NOT rotate).
         - table_rotation_joint (revolute, axis +Z, +-pi) drives
           turntable_link.
         - Both fixtures parent to turntable_link, so they rotate
           with the disc.  Fixture 2 is mounted 180 deg from fixture 1.
         - photoelectric sensor parents to base_link, so it stays
           fixed and only "sees" fixture 1 in the LOAD position.
         - NEMA + belt parent to base_link (motor side) and to
           turntable_link (driven pulley) - both VISUAL only; the
           cinematics is exclusively the table_rotation_joint.
         - Pistons inside fixtures are FIXED (not prismatic) per spec.
         - All debug CAFI / grasp / pick marker visuals were dropped
           from the xacro copy so the planta does not show duplicates
           against object_manager's dynamic CAFIs. -->
  <xacro:turntable_rivet_cell parent="riveting_zone"
                              xyz="0 0 0"
                              rpy="0 0 0"/>

  <!-- ===== V41 Vision zone (DXF #46: 150x151 mm @ (381.5, 215.1)) =====
       V40 instantiated a workstation_table (15 mm grey plate, 150x151)
       to support the fixture_vision STL.  The user flagged that plate
       as "la mesita gris flotante" (zero-length legs made it look like
       a floating plate at z=1.015).  V41 removes the workstation_table
       and mounts the fixture_vision STL DIRECTLY on the mesa top; the
       fixture STL is itself a 15 mm thick cradle plate so it provides
       the visual base.                                                 -->
  <!-- V44: vision zone moved 0.074 m WEST so the cobot has more
       clearance reaching it (reach was OK at V43 but the wrist envelope
       brushed the cradle wall during APPROACH_VISION).  V44 anchor is
       at (0.750, 0.804).  Reach 3D from cobot (1.152, 1.049, 1.000)
       to cradle CAFI centre (0.750, 0.804, 1.0275):
         d = sqrt(0.402^2 + 0.245^2 + 0.028^2) = 0.471 m  (155 mm reach margin) -->
  <link name="vision_zone"/>
  <joint name="world_to_vision_zone" type="fixed">
    <parent link="world"/>
    <child  link="vision_zone"/>
    <origin xyz="0.750 0.804 1.000" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>

  <xacro:fixture_vision name="fixture_2" parent="vision_zone"
                        base_z="0.0" yaw="0"/>

  <!-- ===== V38 Cognex camera HANGING from cabin top ====================
       Camera body directly above the fixture cámara at world (0.824,
       0.804) with the body+lens at z = mesa_top + 0.320 = 1.320 m.
       Suspension column hangs DOWN from the cabin top profile (z=2.07)
       to the body (z=1.32) - arm_length=0 so the column is coaxial
       with the body, no lateral kink.
       The body is pitched +pi/2 about Y so its lens (local +X) points
       straight DOWN at the CAFI on the fixture.                       -->
  <!-- V40: camera raised 200 mm (z = 1.520 instead of 1.320) so the
       cobot wrist envelope does not graze the camera body during
       APPROACH_VISION/PLACE_VISION movements.  Mesa = 1.000, fixture
       cradle top = 1.030, CAFI top on cradle = ~1.058.  At z=1.520,
       lens-to-CAFI distance is 462 mm; still inside the Cognex 2800
       working range (300-700 mm typical).  Column hangs from cabin top
       at z=2.07 down to camera body at z=1.52 (length 550 mm).      -->
  <!-- V44: camera moves WITH the vision fixture (same X shift of 0.074 m
       to the west).  Lens stays coaxial with the cradle CAFI seat.  -->
  <xacro:cognex_2800 name="cognex_camera" parent="world"
                     xy_x="0.750" xy_y="0.804"
                     z="1.520"
                     yaw_to_target="0.0"
                     pitch_to_target="1.5707963267948966"
                     column_top_z="2.070" column_bottom_z="1.520"
                     column_radius="0.012"
                     arm_length="0.0"
                     body_x="0.060" body_y="0.045" body_z="0.045"
                     lens_radius="0.014" lens_length="0.028"/>

  <!-- ===== V38 Lexium L03S mounted DIRECTLY on the mesa ================
       NO external pedestal, NO hanging.  The canonical link0_base.STL
       is the real cobot base plate; it bolts onto the mesa top at the
       mesa centre.  mount_mode="floor" applies Rx(+pi/2) so the CAD
       +Y arm axis maps to world +Z (cobot stands up).
       Anchor:   xy = (1.152, 1.049)   = mesa centre shifted 0.10 m WEST
                  z = 1.000             = mesa top
       Pedestal: HEIGHT=0, RADIUS=0    -> no extra visual added.
       yaw = 0 -> at q=0 the arm extends toward world +X.

       Shift WHY: mesa exact centre (1.252, 1.049) leaves the IK with
       only 0.043 m margin to the disc LOAD position (3D = 0.583 m vs
       L03S reach 0.626 m) so the LOAD/RIVET poses cannot be solved
       within the +/-2 pi joint limits.  Moving the cobot 0.10 m WEST
       (toward the disc) gives the LOAD pose 0.139 m of margin while
       keeping every other station well within reach.  0.10 m is the
       MINIMUM shift that gets all 17 poses to converge - smaller
       shifts still fail PLACE_LOAD_FIXTURE.

       Reach check (3D from (1.152, 1.049, 1.000)):
         conveyor PICK west  (1.235, 1.365, 1.135): d = 0.353
         disc LOAD           (0.692, 1.109, 1.151): d = 0.487
         fixture cámara      (0.824, 0.804, 1.065): d = 0.415
         bin aceptado        (1.411, 0.679, 1.125): d = 0.469
         bin rechazado       (1.110, 0.684, 1.125): d = 0.388                                   -->
  <xacro:lexium_cobot_real name="lexium_cobot" parent="world"
                           xy_x="1.152" xy_y="1.049"
                           base_z="1.000" yaw="0.0"
                           pedestal_height="0.0"
                           pedestal_radius="0.0"
                           mount_mode="floor"/>

  <!-- ===== V37 Aluminum cabin (decorative enclosure) =====================
       V37 cobot is FLOOR mounted; the cabin no longer carries it.
       Cabin remains as a visible enclosure of the work cell with the
       top profile at z=2.07 m.  cobot_mount_* are unused at this
       call site but the macro signature still expects them - we
       point them at a dummy z=2.020 well above the cobot's working
       envelope so the (decorative) flange visual is not seen.     -->
  <xacro:aluminum_cabin name="cabin" parent="world"
                        x_min="0.30" x_max="2.20"
                        y_min="0.30" y_max="1.80"
                        top_z="2.070"
                        cobot_mount_x="0.950"
                        cobot_mount_y="0.972"
                        cobot_mount_z="2.020"/>

  <!-- ===== V36 Gripper (SolidWorks 99.5 mm Z reference aligned) =====
       The user's SolidWorks measurement: the gripper mount centre
       (where the gripper's mounting plate bolts to the cobot flange)
       is 99.5 mm = 0.0995 m along the SW Z axis from the tip of the
       closing tooth (the furthest point of the gripper).
       Y+ is the SolidWorks CAD reference axis (NOT RViz/ROS Y+).
       The conversion from SW to RViz follows the assembly Rx(-pi/2)
       this URDF already applies via ASSEMBLY_RPY in new_gripper.xacro:
         SW Y+ (CAD vertical) -> mesh Y -> after Rx(-pi/2) -> link -Z
         SW Z+ (axial)       -> mesh Z -> after Rx(-pi/2) -> link -Y
       So the SW "99.5 mm along Z" maps to "0.0995 m along link -Y"
       in the gripper_base frame, which corresponds to the Euclidean
       distance from the mounting-plate centre to the appendage tip
       in our URDF:
         appendage tip (link frame, closed)  = (0, +0.056, +0.080)
         stump bottom-face centre            = (0, -0.014,  0.000)
         |tip - centre| = sqrt(0.070^2 + 0.080^2) = 0.1063 m
       The 6 mm Euclidean vs axial difference is mesh-tolerance:
       the SW 99.5 mm is the axial distance along the tool axis;
       our link Y component (0.070 m) is the lateral offset of the
       tooth from the axis.  Setting mount_xyz so the stump bottom
       face centre coincides with tool0:
         mount_xyz = (0, -0.014, 0)  (negates Rz(pi) @ (0,-0.014,0) =
                                       (0, +0.014, 0))
         mount_yaw = pi              (keeps the closing tooth pointing
                                       toward the CAFI when the cobot
                                       is at HOME / PICK pose)
       lexium_kinematics.GRASP_CENTER_OFFSET = (0, +0.014, +0.025) is
       in lock-step (see scripts/lexium_kinematics.py).
       The canonical URDF tool0 frame is NOT touched.                 -->
  <!-- V41: gripper pulled 35 mm IN toward the cobot wrist so the
       64 mm Ø mounting plate sits FLUSH against the visible flange
       disc.  Diagnosis: the canonical link6_tool_flange.STL mesh ends
       at link6_wrist3 Y=+0.033 m (the front face of the flange disc),
       while joint_tool0 origin is at link6_wrist3 Y=+0.068 m; a
       35 mm offset BEYOND the visible disc.  V36-V40 placed the plate
       at tool0 (0, 0, 0), leaving a 35 mm visible air gap between
       the flange disc front face and the plate back face.  V41 fixes
       this: mount_xyz pulls the plate to tool0 (0, -0.035, 0) so the
       plate visibly bolts against the flange disc front face.  XY
       centroid alignment from V40 is preserved (+0.516 mm correction).
       Net mount_xyz Y = -0.01385 (V40 centroid) - 0.0350 (flange pull-
       back) = -0.04885 m.                                            -->
  <!-- V43: gripper is now PART OF the cobot URDF, mounted INSIDE
       lexium_cobot_with_final_gripper.xacro (tool0 -> gripper_base ->
       stump/fixture/fixture1/neck/appendage -> tcp_link).  The working
       TCP frame the rest of the planta uses is
       "lexium_cobot_tcp_grasp_center".  No separate new_gripper macro
       is instantiated.                                                  -->
  <!-- (V42 new_gripper call deleted in V43.) -->


  <!-- ===== V37 Control station (DXF #39 @ (241.6, -126.7) -> world
       (0.684, 0.462), south of the mesa, OUTSIDE the mesa footprint.
       size 0.483 x 0.254 m per DXF.                                  -->
  <xacro:control_station name="control_station" parent="world"
                         xy_x="0.684" xy_y="0.462" yaw="0"
                         width="0.483" depth="0.254" height="1.200"/>

  <!-- ===== Operator chair (preserved) ================================ -->
  <xacro:macro name="operator_chair"
               params="name parent x y seat_size_x seat_size_y
                       seat_top_z backrest_height leg_radius">
    <xacro:property name="seat_thick"  value="0.040"/>
    <xacro:property name="back_thick"  value="0.040"/>
    <xacro:property name="leg_h"       value="${seat_top_z - seat_thick}"/>
    <link name="${name}_seat">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="${seat_size_x} ${seat_size_y} ${seat_thick}"/></geometry>
        <material name="chair_seat_mat"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="${parent}_to_${name}_seat" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${parent}"/>
      <child  link="${name}_seat"/>
      <origin xyz="${x} ${y} ${seat_top_z - seat_thick/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <link name="${name}_back">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="${seat_size_x} ${back_thick} ${backrest_height}"/></geometry>
        <material name="chair_back_mat"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="${name}_seat_to_back" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${name}_seat"/>
      <child  link="${name}_back"/>
      <origin xyz="0 ${-seat_size_y/2 + back_thick/2} ${seat_thick/2 + backrest_height/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <xacro:macro name="_chair_leg" params="suffix dx dy">
      <link name="${name}_leg_${suffix}">
        <visual>
          <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
          <geometry><cylinder radius="${leg_radius}" length="${leg_h}"/></geometry>
          <material name="chair_leg_mat"/>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="${name}_seat_to_leg_${suffix}" type="fixed">
        <parent link="${name}_seat"/>
        <child  link="${name}_leg_${suffix}"/>
        <origin xyz="${dx} ${dy} ${-seat_thick/2 - leg_h/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:macro>
    <xacro:_chair_leg suffix="ff" dx="${ seat_size_x/2 - 0.030}" dy="${-seat_size_y/2 + 0.030}"/>
    <xacro:_chair_leg suffix="fb" dx="${ seat_size_x/2 - 0.030}" dy="${ seat_size_y/2 - 0.030}"/>
    <xacro:_chair_leg suffix="bf" dx="${-seat_size_x/2 + 0.030}" dy="${-seat_size_y/2 + 0.030}"/>
    <xacro:_chair_leg suffix="bb" dx="${-seat_size_x/2 + 0.030}" dy="${ seat_size_y/2 - 0.030}"/>
  </xacro:macro>

  <xacro:operator_chair name="operator_chair" parent="world"
                        x="0.684" y="0.150"
                        seat_size_x="0.400" seat_size_y="0.300"
                        seat_top_z="0.500" backrest_height="0.400"
                        leg_radius="0.018"/>

  <!-- ===== V38 Sensors (repositioned to new layout + west pick) ====== -->
  <!-- Conveyor LEFT pick photoelectric: belt centred at (1.370, 1.365);
       the pick is at world X = 1.235 (west end), so the sensor faces
       NORTH across the belt right at the pick X.                      -->
  <xacro:sick_photoelectric name="sensor_conveyor_end" parent="world"
                            face_x="1.235" face_y="1.290" face_z="1.100"
                            beam_yaw="1.5707963267948966"
                            mesa_z="1.000" beam_len="0.150"/>

  <!-- V52: sensor_rotary_load_fixture REMOVED.  The new turntable URDF
       ships its own photoelectric sensor on a pedestal attached to
       base_link (photoelectric_sensor_pedestal_fixture_1_link ->
       photoelectric_sensor_fixture_1_link with a visible light ray).
       It detects fixture 1 only and does NOT rotate with the disc. -->
  <!-- (V41 sick_photoelectric "sensor_rotary_load_fixture" deleted in V52.) -->

  <!-- Sensor west of vision cradle at world (0.824, 0.804).  Beam
       yaw=0 (west-to-east).                                          -->
  <!-- V44: sensor moves with the vision fixture (shifted west by 0.074 m).  -->
  <xacro:sick_photoelectric name="sensor_vision_piece_present" parent="world"
                            face_x="0.586" face_y="0.804" face_z="1.040"
                            beam_yaw="0.0"
                            mesa_z="1.000" beam_len="0.130"/>

  <!-- ===== V38 Actuators ============================================== -->
  <!-- Conveyor drive motor under EAST end of belt (V38 pick is on west). -->
  <xacro:conveyor_drive_motor name="conveyor_drive_motor" parent="world"
                              xy_x="1.550" xy_y="1.365" z="1.036"
                              axis_yaw="1.5707963267948966"/>

  <!-- V41: rotary_drive macro REMOVED.  V37/V38 installed a NEMA-17 +
       planetary gearbox hanging UNDER the mesa (mesa_bottom_z=0.960
       with the output shaft poking up through the mesa).  The user
       flagged it as "el NEMA esta abajo" - the subterranean NEMA was
       confusing.  V41 keeps ONLY the visible NEMA on top of the disco
       gearbase to the EAST of the disc (the nemabase_1.STL already
       instantiated by rotary_index_table_v37 at link X=+0.244 m =
       world (0.936, 1.259, +0.026) ).  The belt_top + belt_bot
       visuals (V40) connect that NEMA to the central sprocket.     -->

  <!-- ===== V37 Pneumatics ============================================= -->
  <!-- FRL stays south of the mesa, away from the floor-mounted cobot. -->
  <xacro:pneumatic_air_supply name="pneumatic_air_supply" parent="world"
                              xy_x="0.300" xy_y="0.380"
                              base_z="0.0" yaw="0.0"/>

</robot>
